        {
          "id": "SP_ACANTHELLA_VACELETI_VAN_SOEST_STENTOFT_1988",
          "name": "Acanthella vaceleti van Soest & Stentoft, 1988",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Acanthella",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Fig. 42 a) Erect, irregularly bladed growth forms, without stalk. Dimensions of largest specimen 5 x 5 x 5 cm, blades 3 – 5 mm thick. Surface indented with lengthwise grooves. Color (in alcohol) pale beige or brown. Consistency firm but elastic. Skeleton. Of the blades and outgrowths consisting of a thick central axis (Fig. 42 b), 1 – 1.3 mm diameter, of intertwined sinuous strongyles. Extra-axial skeleton consists of outgrowths of the central axis with a mixture of styles and strongyles and many single styles. Spicules. (Figs 42 c – f) Styles, ‘ sinuous’ strongyles. Styles (Figs 42 c – d) smooth, usually curved, with rounded end often slightly narrower than the shaft, but not distinctly fusiform, in a large size range of shorter-thicker (Figs 42 c, c 1) and longer-thinner spicules (Fig. 42 d), but not divisible into clear size categories, 246 – 610 – 1152 x 6 – 17.1 – 39 µm. Sinuous strongyles, smooth, doubly or multiply curved, in a large size range, 481 – 1041 – 1440 x 9 – 11.4 – 14 µm.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:5183034",
          "authorship": "van Soest & Stentoft",
          "yearPublished": "1988",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "4a297e22-c2ca-520-90a-ead51488346ba8",
          "sourceIds": {
